    "sy.h": "🔄 Sync", "sy.sub": "The same lessons, notes and review on your PC and your phone.", "sy.nome": "Sync", "sy.lbl": "Sync", "sy.t": "🔄 PC and phone together", "sy.s": "The same lessons and review on PC and phone, on the same Wi-Fi network.", "sy.apri": "Open…", "sy.mai": "never", "sy.ora": "just now", "sy.min": "{n} min ago", "sy.ore": "{n} hours ago", "sy.giorni": "{n} days ago", "sy.incorso": "Syncing…", "sy.lontano": "Not synced (different network)", "sy.fatto": "Synced {q}", "sy.collegati": "Linked: {a} ↔ {b}. From now on they sync by themselves.", "sy.nontrova.l": "If they can't find each other", "sy.nontrova": "PC and phone must be on the <b>same Wi-Fi network</b>. Many public networks (university Wi-Fi, Eduroam, libraries, cafés) don't let two devices talk to each other: then turn on the <b>phone's hotspot</b> and connect the PC to it (syncing uses no data). Or wait until you're home: it syncs by itself as soon as both are on your home Wi-Fi.", "sy.firewall": "The first time, Windows may ask whether to let Verba Manent IA use the network: choose <b>«Allow»</b> (private networks).", "sy.questopc": "This PC: {n}", "sy.scrivilo": "On the phone: Settings → 🔄 Sync → «Link to PC», then scan the QR (or type the code).", "sy.scade": "The code is valid for {n} more min", "sy.aspetto": "Waiting for the phone…", "sy.collegati.t": "Link to PC", "sy.scrivi": "Type the 6-digit code you see on the PC (Settings → 🔄 Sync → «Link a phone»).", "sy.collega": "Link", "sy.qr": "Scan the PC's QR code", "sy.oppure": "or type the code under the QR", "sy.cerco": "Looking for the PC on the network…", "sy.colltel": "Link a phone", "sy.collpc": "Link to another PC", "sy.una": "You do it once, in 1 minute", "sy.p1": "On the PC: Settings → 🔄 Sync → «Link a phone»", "sy.p1s": "A QR code appears, with a 6-digit code under it.", "sy.p2": "On the phone: Settings → 🔄 Sync → «Link to PC»", "sy.p2s": "Scan the QR (or type the code). PC and phone must be on the same Wi-Fi network (or on the phone's hotspot).", "sy.p3": "Done: «Linked ✓»", "sy.p3s": "From then on, whenever they are on the same network, they exchange lessons, notes, photos and reviews by themselves.", "sy.disp": "Linked devices", "sy.adesso": "Sync now", "sy.altro": "Link another device", "sy.nota.tel": "The phone syncs every minute while the app is open. The PC must be on, with Verba Manent IA open.", "sy.nota.pc": "The phone syncs every minute while its app is open. Keep Verba Manent IA open on the PC (minimised is fine).", "sy.cosa": "What gets synced", "sy.o.lezioni": "Lessons", "sy.o.lezioni.s": "audio, transcript, notes, slides, photos, handwritten notes", "sy.o.studio": "Study", "sy.o.studio.s": "daily review, flashcards, multiple choice, tutor", "sy.o.materie": "Subjects", "sy.o.materie.s": "exam dates, test and oral marks, study plan, glossary, test map", "sy.o.libro": "Textbook", "sy.o.libro.s": "the text that was read (the PDF stays where it is)", "sy.o.video": "Lesson videos", "sy.o.video.s": "heavy (up to 1 GB each): usually not needed on the phone, the audio is enough", "sy.unisce": "If the same thing changes on two devices (e.g. review done on both), the program merges without losing anything. A lesson deleted on one device is deleted on the others too.", "sy.ancora": "not synced yet", "sy.scollega": "Unlink", "sy.scollega.d": "{n} will no longer sync with this device. The lessons stay where they are. To link it again you need a new code.", "sy.err.lontano": "I can't find the PC on the network: it will sync by itself as soon as you're on the same Wi-Fi.", "sy.err.rete": "The last sync didn't work. I'll try again in a minute.", "sy.attesa.c": "First sync in a moment…", "sy.attesa.s": "Waiting for the phone to sync (it happens when its app is open).", "sy.ultimo": "Last time: {a} files received, {m} sent, {u} merged.",
    "nv.lbl": "Away from home too", "nv.collegato": "Linked to {p}: {e}", "nv.browser": "Finish signing in in the browser that just opened…", "nv.manca": "There are already zips made by another device in the cloud. Type their password: you'll find it on the other device in Settings › Sync.", "nv.ok": "OK", "nv.scollega": "Unlink the cloud", "nv.scollega.d": "This device will stop using the cloud. The zips stay in the cloud and the lessons here stay where they are.", "nv.incorso": "Syncing with the cloud…", "nv.err.accesso": "Cloud access is no longer valid (account password changed or permission removed). Press «Sign in again».", "nv.err.chiave": "The zip password doesn't match the zips in the cloud. Unlink the cloud and link it again typing the right password.", "nv.err.dati": "You are on mobile data: the cloud waits for Wi-Fi (untick below to use data too).", "nv.err.rete": "The last cloud sync didn't work. I'll try again in 10 minutes.", "nv.fatto": "In the cloud: synced {q}", "nv.ultimo": "{s} lessons uploaded, {g} downloaded", "nv.primo": "First cloud sync in a moment…", "nv.chiave": "The zip password", "nv.chiave.s": "Write it on paper and keep it: you only need it if you lose PC and phone together, to reopen the zips from the cloud with 7-Zip. The phone linked with the QR gets it by itself.", "nv.wifi": "On the phone, only on Wi-Fi", "nv.wifi.s": "so it uses no data; untick to sync on mobile data too", "nv.riaccedi": "Sign in again", "nv.adesso": "Sync now", "nv.spiega": "When PC and phone are not on the same network (you at university, the PC at home), lessons go through your cloud: <b>each lesson becomes a password-locked zip</b>. The cloud only sees zip files it can't open. The program only sees the files it creates.", "nv.quale": "Which cloud do you use?", "nv.g.s": "15 GB free (shared with Gmail and Photos)", "nv.m.s": "5 GB free · 1 TB with Microsoft 365", "nv.acc.g": "Sign in with Google", "nv.acc.m": "Sign in with Microsoft", "nv.presto": "The link to this cloud comes with the next update.", "nv.err.annullato": "Sign-in wasn't completed. Try again.", "nv.err.tempo": "5 minutes passed without completing sign-in. Try again.", "nv.contro": "Good to know: one hour of lesson takes 30–60 MB (about 250 hours fit in Drive's 15 GB); videos don't go to the cloud; on mobile data it uses data. On the same Wi-Fi they use Wi-Fi.",
    "rp.anki": "⬇ Export for Anki", "rp.anki.ok": "{n} flashcards exported", "rp.anki.tel": "{n} flashcards ready: choose AnkiDroid to open them", "rp.anki.aperto": "Anki is opening and imports them into the «Verba Manent IA» deck. If you export again after new lessons, Anki updates the cards it already has, with no duplicates and without losing your reviews.", "rp.anki.manca": "I showed you the file in its folder. If Anki isn't installed, download it free from apps.ankiweb.net and then double-click the file.",
    "pc.s.uno": "One voice", "pc.s.due": "Two voices", "pc.s.dib": "Debate", "pc.s.uno.s": "A narrator links the pieces; at the key moments the lecturer speaks, with their real voice.", "pc.s.due.s": "Two study friends: <b>{a}</b> asks the questions you would ask, <b>{b}</b> explains. At the important points they stop and let <b>the lecturer speak, with their real voice</b>.", "pc.s.dib.s": "<b>{a}</b> and <b>{b}</b> argue two opposite ideas on a point of the lesson; the lecturer referees with their real voice, and at the end they say what to answer in the exam.", "pc.prof.reg": "The lecturer, from the recording", "pc.prova.due": "Try «Two voices»",
